# The preset policy in kgsm-base decides whether this daemon runs on a node; applying it is symlink
# manipulation on disk, so it works during the transaction and in a chroot alike. Starting it is the
# node's post-transaction hook's job, which is where a running system is available.
#
# post_install only. An administrator who disabled this unit keeps it disabled across every later
# version — re-presetting on upgrade would quietly undo that.

post_install() {
    systemctl preset kgsm-monitor.service >/dev/null 2>&1 || true

    cat <<'MSG'

  kgsm-monitor needs no configuration: /etc/kgsm-monitor/kgsm-monitor.env holds overrides only, and
  host metrics need nothing from the rest of the ecosystem.

  Per-server metrics are the additive half: they appear once kgsm is installed, since listing the
  instances is what gives the sampler a watch-list. Per-server network rx/tx needs
  kgsm-monitor-net-meter as well; without it those two fields read null — not measured, which is
  the honest answer and never a fabricated 0.

MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
    cat <<'MSG'

  If pacman wrote a .pacnew beside /etc/kgsm-monitor/kgsm-monitor.env, merge it — new settings are
  declared there and a key the file never declares binds to nothing.

MSG
}
